-Two paid physical gear routes; no timer-created animals or rerolled catches.
+Rules126 candidate design (agent choices): make a net from three fibre and
+two wood, or a deadfall trap from three fibre and four wood, at the timber yard
+for 180 work. Carry the physical tool, place it with 80 work at a personally
+known fish spot or woodland tree, leave it for 600 ticks, then return for a
+40-work check. Nets move at most two unreserved fish from that actual source;
+traps make one deterministic attempt against an actual nearby deer and create
+its ordinary carcass. No animal is created by the gear. Checking never rerolls.
+The same equipment registry, pile container, production and activity owners
+hold the gear and catch. One deployed item of each kind per setter is an
+execution cap; remembered owned gear suppresses replacement demand. Each set
+costs ten condition points; a 60-work repair consumes one fibre and restores
+40 points. Resetting costs 40 work. Fish catches expire after 1,200 ticks;
+gear abandoned for 48,000 ticks is lost and accounted. All numbers are bounded
+candidate parameters to test. Viewer evidence must expose the actual wait,
+catch, condition, ownership and empty/broken failures.
 
